   "source": [
    "import requests\n",
    "\n",
    "# Look for teams missing conferences on some rows\n",
    "team_conf = all_stats.assign(has_conf=all_stats[\"conference\"].notna()).groupby([\"season\", \"team\"])[\"has_conf\"].mean()\n",
    "mixed = ((team_conf > 0) & (team_conf < 1)).sum() # Counts each team (by season) that falls between 0 and 1\n",
    "print(f\"Team-seasons with a conference on only some rows: {mixed}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find the conferences listed in the most recent season\n",
    "print(f\"\\nConferences represented in 2026: {sorted(all_stats.loc[(all_stats[\"season\"] == 2026) & all_stats[\"conference\"].notna(), \"conference\"].unique())}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Make sure ESPN-ranked transfers' new schools have a conference listed\n",
    "teams_with_conf = all_stats[all_stats[\"conference\"].notna()][\"team\"].unique() # Teams that have a conference listed\n",
    "no_conf = ~espn_rankings[\"new_school\"].isin(teams_with_conf) # True if the new school has no conference\n",
    "print(f\"\\nESPN-ranked transfers: {len(espn_rankings)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"New schools with no conference listed: {no_conf.sum()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compare to the NCAA's official D1 men's basketball directory (skipped if the website can't be reached)\n",
    "d1_2026_teams = all_stats[(all_stats[\"season\"] == 2026) & all_stats[\"conference\"].notna()] # Our D1 teams in the most recent season\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    response = requests.get(\"https://web3.ncaa.org/directory/api/directory/memberList\",\n",
    "                            params={\"type\": 12, \"division\": \"I\", \"sportCode\": \"MBB\"}, timeout=30)\n",
    "    response.raise_for_status()\n",
    "    ncaa_d1 = pd.DataFrame(response.json())\n",
    "    ncaa_d1 = ncaa_d1[ncaa_d1[\"division\"] == 1] # Keep only Division I\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nNCAA D1 teams: {len(ncaa_d1)}, teams with a conference in our data (2026): {d1_2026_teams['team'].nunique()}\")\n",
    "except requests.RequestException:\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nCould not reach the NCAA directory, so this comparison was skipped. Teams with a conference in our data (2026): {d1_2026_teams['team'].nunique()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Look through teams without a conference across all seasons\n",
    "no_conf = (\n",
    "    all_stats[all_stats[\"conference\"].isna()]\n",
    "    .groupby(\"team\").size().sort_index()\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n{len(no_conf)} teams without a conference across all season:\")\n",
    "print(no_conf.index.tolist())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c13b1acc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We define a Division I school as a team with a `conference` listed in that season, since the API only fills in this field for D1 programs. This held up in all the checks we ran. No team has a conference on only some of its rows, all 31 listed conferences are D1 conferences, and we did a manual review of the 367 teams that have a conference in any season, finding no D2 or D3 programs. All 600 schools in ESPN's transfer rankings have a conference listed, and the 365 teams with a conference in our 2026 data match the NCAA's 365 listed D1 programs. Finally, we did a manual review of the 763 teams without a conference across all seasons and found no D1 schools, except for schools such as Lindenwood, Queens, Mercyhurst, and East Texas A&M, who moved up to D1 throughout the time period. Because a school's status can change, we will apply this definition separately for each season."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9cfd30d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Keep only D1 transfers**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 44,
   "id": "filter-d1-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Prior school D1 vs. new school D1:\n",
      "new_school_d1    False  True \n",
      "prior_school_d1              \n",
      "False              277    156\n",
      "True               220   5541\n",
      "\n",
      "Transfers before filter: 6194\n",
      "Transfers to a D1 school: 5697\n",
      "\n",
      "Transfers to D1 by season:\n",
      "season\n",
      "2021     445\n",
      "2022     832\n",
      "2023     822\n",
      "2024     950\n",
      "2025    1215\n",
      "2026    1433\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# D1 teams are the ones with a conference listed\n",
    "transfers[\"new_school_d1\"] = transfers[\"conference_this_year\"].notna()\n",
    "transfers[\"prior_school_d1\"] = transfers[\"conference_last_year\"].notna()\n",
    "transfers[\"prior_school_division\"] = transfers[\"prior_school_d1\"].map({True: \"D1\", False: \"Not D1\"}) # Label the prior school as D1 or not D1\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Prior school D1 vs. new school D1:\")\n",
    "print(pd.crosstab(transfers[\"prior_school_d1\"], transfers[\"new_school_d1\"]))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep only transfers who ended up at a D1 school\n",
    "transfers_d1 = transfers[transfers[\"new_school_d1\"]].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTransfers before filter: {len(transfers)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Transfers to a D1 school: {len(transfers_d1)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTransfers to D1 by season:\\n{transfers_d1['season'].value_counts().sort_index()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "92a0a89a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Of the 6,194 transfers, 5,697 (92%) ended up at a D1 school, so the filter removed 497 players who moved to a non-D1 school (277 from a non-D1 school and 220 from a D1 school). Of the 5,697 D1 transfers, 5,541 also came from a D1 school and 156 (about 3%) moved up from a lower division. We keep those 156, but their prior-season stats come from a different level of competition, so we created a `prior_school_division` column that flags whether the transfer came from a D1 school or not. The number of D1 transfers grows from 445 in 2021 to 1,433 in 2026, so later seasons make up most of the data (the 2025 and 2026 seasons together are about 47%)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e0a1714d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Join the ESPN preseason rankings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 45,
   "id": "17dc7314",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Joins where the new school disagrees: 2\n",
      "\n",
      "ESPN-ranked transfers (2022-2026): 500\n",
      "Matched to a transfer in our data: 476\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Clean player names so ESPN's names and the API's names match more often\n",
    "def clean_name(series):\n",
    "    return (series.str.normalize(\"NFKD\").str.encode(\"ascii\", \"ignore\").str.decode(\"ascii\") # Remove accents\n",
    "            .str.lower()\n",
    "            .str.replace(r\"[^a-z ]\", \"\", regex=True) # D.J. becomes dj\n",
    "            .str.replace(r\"\\b(jr|sr|ii|iii|iv)\\b\", \"\", regex=True) # Drop suffixes like Jr.\n",
    "            .str.split().str.join(\" \")) # Remove extra spaces\n",
    "\n",
    "espn = espn_rankings[espn_rankings[\"year\"] <= 2026].copy() # Leave out 2026-27 class since they have barely played\n",
    "espn[\"name_key\"] = clean_name(espn[\"player\"])\n",
    "transfers_d1[\"name_key\"] = clean_name(transfers_d1[\"name_this_year\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "rows_before = len(transfers_d1)\n",
    "transfers_d1 = transfers_d1.merge(\n",
    "    espn[[\"name_key\", \"year\", \"espn_preseason_rank\", \"new_school\"]].rename(columns={\"year\": \"season\", \"new_school\": \"espn_new_school\"}),\n",
    "    on=[\"name_key\", \"season\"], how=\"left\") # Left join keeps alls transfer including unranked players\n",
    "assert len(transfers_d1) == rows_before, \"The join duplicated rows\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Make sure the new school agrees with ESPN rankings since multiple players can have the same name\n",
    "wrong_player = transfers_d1[\"espn_preseason_rank\"].notna() & (transfers_d1[\"espn_new_school\"] != transfers_d1[\"team_this_year\"])\n",
    "print(f\"Joins where the new school disagrees: {wrong_player.sum()}\")\n",
    "transfers_d1.loc[wrong_player, \"espn_preseason_rank\"] = np.nan # Remove the rank for any wrongs player\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nESPN-ranked transfers (2022-2026): {len(espn)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Matched to a transfer in our data: {transfers_d1['espn_preseason_rank'].notna().sum()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find the ESPN players that didn't match\n",
    "matched = transfers_d1.loc[transfers_d1[\"espn_preseason_rank\"].notna(), [\"name_key\", \"season\"]]\n",
    "unmatched = espn.merge(matched, left_on=[\"name_key\", \"year\"], right_on=[\"name_key\", \"season\"], how=\"left\", indicator=True)\n",
    "unmatched = unmatched[unmatched[\"_merge\"] == \"left_only\"].copy()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c2cde11e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "ESPN ranked 600 transfers across six classes, but because the 2026-27 class (100 players) is just starting, we kept 500 rankings from 2022 to 2026. We matched 476 of them to a transfer in our data using a cleaned version of the player name and the season. Two matches had a different new school than ESPN listed, so they were two different players with the same name, and we removed their ranks. 24 of the 500 ESPN-ranked players did not match a transfer in our data, which is most likely due to the player being missing from the API data from the season before or after the transfer, which is a potential limitation to our analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a2334095",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Create the starter variable (the target)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 46,
   "id": "ef516a44",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Players with 0 games at the new school: 0\n",
      "Starters: 3005 of 5697 (52.7%)\n",
      "\n",
      "Share of starters by season:\n",
      "season\n",
      "2021    0.481\n",
      "2022    0.542\n",
      "2023    0.534\n",
      "2024    0.517\n",
      "2025    0.532\n",
      "2026    0.533\n",
      "Name: starter, dtype: float64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Share of games he started at his new school, and the target (started more than half of his games)\n",
    "transfers_d1[\"start_rate\"] = transfers_d1[\"starts_this_year\"] / transfers_d1[\"games_this_year\"]\n",
    "transfers_d1[\"starter\"] = (transfers_d1[\"start_rate\"] > 0.5).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Players with 0 games at the new school: {(transfers_d1['games_this_year'] == 0).sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Starters: {transfers_d1['starter'].sum()} of {len(transfers_d1)} ({transfers_d1['starter'].mean():.1%})\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nShare of starters by season:\\n{transfers_d1.groupby('season')['starter'].mean().round(3)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c62e0992",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We define a starter as a player who started more than half of his games at the new school. Every transfer played at least one game, so the start rate is always defined. 3,005 of the 5,697 transfers (52.7%) are starters. Interestingly, the percentage of transfer starters is similar each season (48% to 54%). "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b6968468",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Remove players who don't play enough games"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 47,
   "id": "193cf82f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "1 games: 5697 players, 52.7% starters\n",
      "5 games: 5509 players, 54.2% starters\n",
      "10 games: 5193 players, 56.2% starters\n",
      "15 games: 4890 players, 58.3% starters\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
