      ],
      "source": [
        "percentages = [\"fieldGoals/pct_last_year\", \"twoPointFieldGoals/pct_last_year\", \"threePointFieldGoals/pct_last_year\", \"freeThrows/pct_last_year\",\n",
        "            \"effectiveFieldGoalPct_last_year\", \"trueShootingPct_last_year\", \"offensiveReboundPct_last_year\", \"usage_last_year\"] # Pull all the percentage columns\n",
        "display(transfers_d1[percentages].describe().T[[\"min\", \"50%\", \"max\"]])\n",
        "\n",
        "shot_types = [\"fieldGoals\", \"twoPointFieldGoals\", \"threePointFieldGoals\", \"freeThrows\"] # Shooting percentages\n",
        "\n",
        "for shot in shot_types:\n",
        "    zero_pct = transfers_d1[f\"{shot}/pct_last_year\"] == 0 # Players with a 0% shooting percentage\n",
        "    no_shots = transfers_d1[f\"{shot}/attempted_last_year\"] == 0 # Players who took no shots of this type\n",
        "    print(f\"{shot}: {zero_pct.sum()} players with 0%, {(zero_pct & no_shots).sum()} took no shots, {(zero_pct & ~no_shots).sum()} took shots and missed them all\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 24,
      "id": "ec3fe486",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ec3fe486"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "for shot in shot_types:\n",
        "    no_shots = transfers_d1[f\"{shot}/attempted_last_year\"] == 0 # Players who took no shots of this type\n",
        "    transfers_d1.loc[no_shots, f\"{shot}/pct_last_year\"] = np.nan # No attempts means the percentage is unknown, not 0\n",
        "\n",
        "transfers_d1[\"trueShootingPct_last_year\"] = transfers_d1[\"trueShootingPct_last_year\"] * 100"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "2960354f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2960354f"
      },
      "source": [
        "True shooting percentage was a fraction (with a median of about 0.54), even though all the other percentages are out of 100. True shooting percentage can go above 100% because it measures points per shot attempt, scaled so that 100% means 2 points per attempt (a made 3 pointer is 3 points on 1 shot attempt, which is 150%). We multiplied this column by 100 to match the other percentages.\n",
        "\n",
        "The data also reported a 0% shooting percentage for players who took no shots as well as for players who took shots and missed them all, and these mean two different things about the player. We changed the percentage to NaN for the players who didn't take any shots (42 for field goals, 83 for two pointers, 654 for three pointers and 291 for free throws). There were no NaN values in these four shooting percentages before this cleaning."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "887984db",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "887984db"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Create the feature variables"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "3e35ddd4",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3e35ddd4"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Convert raw stats to per game**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 25,
      "id": "b01a4447",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b01a4447"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "raw_stats = [\"points\", \"assists\", \"steals\", \"blocks\", \"turnovers\", \"fouls\", \"rebounds/total\", \"rebounds/offensive\", \"rebounds/defensive\",\n",
        "               \"fieldGoals/attempted\", \"threePointFieldGoals/attempted\", \"freeThrows/attempted\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "per_game_features = []\n",
        "for stat in raw_stats: # Loop through stats and replace them with per game metrics\n",
        "    name = stat.replace(\"/\", \"_\") + \"_per_game_last_year\"\n",
        "    transfers_d1[name] = transfers_d1[f\"{stat}_last_year\"] / transfers_d1[\"games_last_year\"]\n",
        "    per_game_features.append(name)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Win shares per game (the API only gives the per 40 version for the total, so we keep that one as is)\n",
        "for ws in [\"offensive\", \"defensive\"]:\n",
        "    transfers_d1[f\"winShares_{ws}_per_game_last_year\"] = transfers_d1[f\"winShares/{ws}_last_year\"] / transfers_d1[\"games_last_year\"]\n",
        "    per_game_features.append(f\"winShares_{ws}_per_game_last_year\")\n",
        "\n",
        "transfers_d1[\"minutes_per_game_last_year\"] = transfers_d1[\"minutes_last_year\"] / transfers_d1[\"games_last_year\"] # Minutes per game at prior school\n",
        "transfers_d1[\"start_rate_last_year\"] = transfers_d1[\"starts_last_year\"] / transfers_d1[\"games_last_year\"] # Share of games he started at prior school\n",
        "transfers_d1[\"prior_school_d1\"] = transfers_d1[\"prior_school_d1\"].astype(int) # 1 if the prior school was D1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "dc46b1ed",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dc46b1ed"
      },
      "source": [
        "Because raw season totals (such as points, assists, steals, etc.) depend on how much a player plays, we converted them to per game averages. We also added minutes per game and start rate at the prior school as two other potential candidates for feature variables."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 26,
      "id": "9c76e814",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "9c76e814",
        "outputId": "c36db2e8-319e-440e-94c9-47c775631336"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "position_last_year\n",
            "G      3105\n",
            "F      2009\n",
            "C       329\n",
            "ATH      38\n",
            "PG       16\n",
            "SG        7\n",
            "SF        3\n",
