          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "print(transfers_d1[\"position_last_year\"].value_counts(dropna=False)) # How many players at each position\n",
        "\n",
        "print(transfers_d1.groupby(\"position_last_year\")[\"starter\"].agg([\"count\", \"mean\"]).round(3)) # Players and share of starters by position"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "1be0e13c",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1be0e13c"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Deal with positions**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 27,
      "id": "3e0f1c02",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "3e0f1c02",
        "outputId": "56b4e188-17da-4778-d1cb-2477a98cb80c"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "position_group\n",
            "G        3128\n",
            "F        2014\n",
            "C         329\n",
            "Other      38\n",
            "Name: count, dtype: int64\n",
            "  position_last_year position_group  pos_C  pos_F  pos_G  pos_Other\n",
            "0                  G              G      0      0      1          0\n",
            "1                  C              C      1      0      0          0\n",
            "2                  F              F      0      1      0          0\n",
            "3                  G              G      0      0      1          0\n",
            "4                  G              G      0      0      1          0\n",
            "5                  F              F      0      1      0          0\n",
            "6                  G              G      0      0      1          0\n",
            "7                  G              G      0      0      1          0\n",
            "8                  G              G      0      0      1          0\n",
            "9                  G              G      0      0      1          0\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "position_groups = {\"G\": \"G\", \"PG\": \"G\", \"SG\": \"G\", \"F\": \"F\", \"SF\": \"F\", \"PF\": \"F\", \"C\": \"C\", \"ATH\": \"Other\"} # How positions will be grouped\n",
        "transfers_d1[\"position_group\"] = transfers_d1[\"position_last_year\"].map(position_groups) # Map to position groups\n",
        "print(transfers_d1[\"position_group\"].value_counts())\n",
        "\n",
        "position_dummies = pd.get_dummies(transfers_d1[\"position_group\"], prefix=\"pos\").astype(int)\n",
        "transfers_d1 = pd.concat([transfers_d1, position_dummies], axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(transfers_d1[[\"position_last_year\", \"position_group\", \"pos_C\", \"pos_F\", \"pos_G\", \"pos_Other\"]].head(10))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "543e6dc2",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "543e6dc2"
      },
      "source": [
        "Some positions were more specific and much rarer (only 16 point guards, 7 shooting guards, 3 small forwards and 2 power forwards, compared to 3,105 guards and 2,009 forwards), so we grouped them into the larger buckets (PG and SG into G, SF and PF into F). We kept C as its own group, and the 38 players listed as ATH (athlete, which is not a standard position) as \"Other.\" Then we one-hot encoded the column for each group so the models can use position as potential feature variable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "9ce0fd75",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9ce0fd75"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Build the feature candidates and check missing values"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 28,
      "id": "14838782",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "14838782",
        "outputId": "6469c64f-ea4c-43ed-b17e-4389c27ca9aa"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Candidate predictors: 37\n",
            "\n",
            "Missing values in the candidate predictors (rows: 5509):\n",
            "                                        Missing Count  Missing Percentage\n",
            "threePointFieldGoals/pct_last_year                654               11.87\n",
            "freeThrows/pct_last_year                          291                5.28\n",
            "assistsTurnoverRatio_last_year                    170                3.09\n",
            "twoPointFieldGoals/pct_last_year                   83                1.51\n",
            "offensiveReboundPct_last_year                      71                1.29\n",
            "winShares_offensive_per_game_last_year             53                0.96\n",
            "netRating_last_year                                53                0.96\n",
            "winShares/totalPer40_last_year                     53                0.96\n",
            "offensiveRating_last_year                          43                0.78\n",
            "PORPAG_last_year                                   43                0.78\n",
            "effectiveFieldGoalPct_last_year                    42                0.76\n",
            "fieldGoals/pct_last_year                           42                0.76\n",
            "freeThrowRate_last_year                            42                0.76\n",
            "trueShootingPct_last_year                          34                0.62\n",
            "winShares_defensive_per_game_last_year             16                0.29\n",
            "defensiveRating_last_year                          16                0.29\n",
            "usage_last_year                                     5                0.09\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "role_features = [\"games_last_year\", \"minutes_per_game_last_year\", \"start_rate_last_year\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "shooting_features = [\"fieldGoals/pct_last_year\", \"twoPointFieldGoals/pct_last_year\", \"threePointFieldGoals/pct_last_year\", \"freeThrows/pct_last_year\",\n",
        "                     \"effectiveFieldGoalPct_last_year\", \"trueShootingPct_last_year\", \"freeThrowRate_last_year\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "advanced_features = [\"offensiveRating_last_year\", \"defensiveRating_last_year\", \"netRating_last_year\", \"PORPAG_last_year\", \"usage_last_year\",\n",
        "                     \"assistsTurnoverRatio_last_year\", \"offensiveReboundPct_last_year\", \"winShares/totalPer40_last_year\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "context_features = [\"prior_school_d1\"] + list(position_dummies.columns) # Add prior school division to position hot-encoded columns\n",
        "\n",
        "candidate_features = role_features + per_game_features + shooting_features + advanced_features + context_features # Build the candidate features list\n",
        "print(f\"Candidate predictors: {len(candidate_features)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "missing = transfers_d1[candidate_features].isna().sum()\n",
        "missing = missing[missing > 0].sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
        "print(f\"\\nMissing values in the candidate predictors (rows: {len(transfers_d1)}):\")\n",
        "print(pd.DataFrame({\"Missing Count\": missing, \"Missing Percentage\": (missing / len(transfers_d1) * 100).round(2)}))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "f253c5ae",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f253c5ae"
      },
      "source": [
        "We kept 37 prior-season columns as potential feature variables to help predict our target. We will use this list of candidate features to determine which best predicts starting role at a player's new school. 16 of the 37 candidate predictors have missing values. Most of the missing values come from the shooting percentages we set to missing for players who took no shots of that type (654 for three pointers, 291 for free throws, 83 for two pointers and 42 for field goals). The rest are advanced stats such as assist to turnover ratio (170 missing), offensive rebound percentage (71) and the ratings (16 to 53 each). No other predictor is missing more than 1% of its rows.\n",
        "\n",
        "We will fill in these missing values during our data modeling process so that we can impute them with the median of our training dataset after the training and test split. This ensures that test data isn't used to pick the imputed value. We chose to impute with the median because it allows us to preserve all players in our data versus dropping whole rows for single missing values, and since it is not impacted by extreme values (for example, a player with very few attempts can have a shooting percentage of 0% or 100%). We set shooting percentages to missing, instead of 0%, for players who took no shots of that type, since they had no shooting record to measure. The assist to turnover ratio is also undefined for the 170 players with no turnovers, and these players played a median of only 4 games last year. We will also include a column marking which values were missing when we impute them.\n",
        "\n",
        "Our final data cleaning step is to scale the features, because they are on very different scales (points per game versus percentages versus ratings) and we don't want one feature to dominate the others just because its numbers are larger. We do this inside the model pipelines so the scaler is fit only on the training data. kNN's distance calculation would be dominated by whichever feature has the largest numbers. When determining the lasso penalty, we also need to scale, because the penalty shrinks coefficients and a coefficient's size depends on the feature's units, so unscaled features would be penalized unevenly for reasons that have nothing to do with how useful they are. We use standard scaling to standardize the features."
      ]
    },
