      "source": [
        "This step computes summary statistics (mean, standard deviation, median, skewness, minimum, and maximum) across numeric features in candidate_features, ranks them by absolute skewness, and plots six histograms for core workload and production metrics (minutes_per_game_last_year, start_rate_last_year, points_per_game_last_year, assists_per_game_last_year, rebounds_total_per_game_last_year, and usage_last_year). Skewness is highest in outlier-heavy rate and binary metrics such as winShares/totalPer40_last_year (71.038), winShares_offensive_per_game_last_year (33.713), pos_Other (11.919), prior_school_d1 (-6.010), and freeThrowRate_last_year (4.195). Visually, the histograms show left skew for minutes per game (peaking around 28 to 32 minutes), U-shaped spikes near 0.0 and 1.0 for prior start rate, right skew for points, assists, and rebounds per game, and a roughly bell-shaped distribution for usage around 18% to 22%, motivating median imputation, feature scaling, and potential non-linear transforms."
      ]
